{"title":"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute-angled triangle whose side lengths satisfy the inequalities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a252cc19c08fe62efc73a6ae674fc651405ca92f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &lt; AC &lt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />. If point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the inscribed circle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the circumscribed circle, prove that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f85e8c5408e12d1e17e232001b1d0613ab674a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IO$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> intersects segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed with barycentrics. First, note that the desired conclusion is equivalent to showing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b9487e47889404e34789d9923927087228178898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=\\overleftrightarrow{IO} \\cap \\overleftrightarrow{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"21\" /> is not on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/9884434c776ea383ad40f494347362443f00db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=(a:0:t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />, so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926a22a52f60bf82b8147e5d19436084da18d1ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 = \\begin{vmatrix} a &amp; 0 &amp; t \\\\ a &amp; b &amp; c \\\\ a^2S_A &amp; b^2S_B &amp; c^2S_C \\end{vmatrix} = abc \\begin{vmatrix} 1 &amp; 0 &amp; \\frac{t}{c} \\\\ 1 &amp; 1 &amp; 1 \\\\ aS_A &amp; bS_B &amp; cS_C \\end{vmatrix} \\implies t=\\frac{c(cS_C-bS_B)}{aS_A-bS_B}\\]\" width=\"569\" height=\"65\" />\nBut, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca8a0979c140028a54225e40e6796a2c2649104b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t = \\frac{c(cS_C-bS_B)}{aS_A-bS_B}=\\frac{c(c(a^2+b^2-c^2)-b(a^2+c^2-b^2))}{a(b^2+c^2-a^2)-b(a^2+c^2-b^2)}=\\frac{c(c-b)(a^2+b^2+c^2)}{(a-b)(a^2+b^2+c^2)}=\\frac{c(c-b)}{a-b} &lt; 0\\]\" width=\"755\" height=\"44\" />\nas needed.\n</p><p>-sillybone\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the lines that pass through the circumcenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac69127bb7a97d71d1cf903e964140436bea116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, respectively.\n</p><p>We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f85e8c5408e12d1e17e232001b1d0613ab674a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IO$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> passes through sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> belongs to either regions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0eee343e73a0dd5b6097194d87d314a6484ff98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4097e707215c7c2085c3fd539de4c228d44f1880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a190cdcd6e20e6dd05262eaad162ab5db648bd6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO = BO = CO = R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"174\" height=\"14\" />, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc2b9b872ca7fabb62cd4f5f8d4b1f660d6c50a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\angle OAC = \\angle OCA$\" width=\"170\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afeede4074ec8d30524c74ccc2691a81c83384d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta = \\angle BAO = \\angle ABO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf46c88adc88cefa236b34b3542256dcecb52ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma = \\angle BCO = \\angle CBO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/9650d2e241cd2ecebf7c294202453c0e975fc5bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; b &lt; a\\implies C &lt; B &lt; A\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"253\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f863e8ad09b3295bf2534074a81d72c33a6adb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma+\\alpha &lt;\\beta+\\gamma &lt;\\alpha+\\beta\\implies\\gamma &lt;\\alpha &lt;\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"312\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f70416d14a373677c13bb4a45d204e5229a1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IA$\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> divides angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> into two equal parts, it must be in the region marked by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d26814d18c58880c417c280a1be37350be9c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in their intersection, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0eee343e73a0dd5b6097194d87d314a6484ff98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. From above, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f85e8c5408e12d1e17e232001b1d0613ab674a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IO$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO\" title=\"1989 USAMO\">1989 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016192648\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 295/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8978/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.456      1 -total\n 52.19%    7.023      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 46.16%    6.212      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5569:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016192648 and revision id 286731. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}